      "content": "4.1 Central Processing Unit (CPU)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Central Processing Unit (CPU) acts as the brain of the computer, executing instructions and managing computations.",
        "The Motherboard serves as the main printed circuit board connecting the CPU, memory, expansion cards, and external peripherals.",
        "Computer ports enable external peripheral devices to communicate directly with the internal hardware.",
        "Expansion cards provide modular upgrades such as enhanced graphics, audio processing, and network interfaces."
